==========================================
DAY 13 NOTES — Loops & Functions
Date: 14-09-2026
==========================================

WHAT I LEARNED TODAY:
- for loop = repeat for each item in a KNOWN list (names, numbers, files)
- while loop = repeat UNTIL a condition becomes false
- {1..5} expands to 1 2 3 4 5 inside a for loop
- Functions package logic once so you can reuse it without copy-pasting
- $1, $2, etc. inside a function = the arguments passed to THAT function call
- Functions must be DEFINED before they're called (bash reads top to bottom)
- Forgetting to update a while loop's counter causes an infinite loop (Ctrl+C to escape)

COMMANDS I PRACTICED:
[ ] for loop over a list
[ ] for loop over a number range {1..5}
[ ] while loop with a counter
[ ] defining a function
[ ] function with an argument ($1)
[ ] calling a function inside a loop

fill this in after running commands yourself :
$ ./greet_all.sh (for loop over names)
> 

$ ./countdown.sh (while loop)
> 

$ ./check.sh (function with if condition)
> 


